{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqa3j03bqhi","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"KB note authoring: 3 rules — override signal, standalone tokens, provenance wiring","summary":"Three mandatory standards for authoring KB note nodes in this workspace:\n\n1. OVERRIDE SIGNAL: When a note contradicts the spec or existing code, the title MUST start with `OVERRIDE:` or the summary must start with `SPEC IS INCOMPLETE:`. This prefix signals that the note takes priority over the spec/code and agents must not dismiss the discrepancy.\n\n2. STANDALONE TOKENS IN TITLE: Note titles must use isolated vocabulary matching agent query patterns — NOT camelCase compounds or hyphenated phrases. Write \"task transcript\" not \"taskTranscript\", \"time window overlap\" not \"time-window-overlap\". Word boundaries matter for the embedding tokenizer; fused tokens degrade retrieval recall.\n\n3. PROVENANCE WIRING: Agents creating notes MUST pass `wires_to=[current_task_key]` in `record_decision` so the DAG edge is created at note-creation time. Do not rely on cosine autowire — it is best-effort and misses structurally important edges. Example: working task #17 → pass `wires_to=[\"17\"]`.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-11T22:55:38.039Z","vec":[-0.15007255971431732,-0.02101985737681389,-0.032059360295534134,-0.03750499710440636,-0.012802870012819767,0.024397891014814377,0.046863675117492676,0.06440677493810654,-0.029501667246222496,0.02152157574892044,0.019120100885629654,-0.02730063535273075,-0.01420590654015541,0.017466487362980843,0.024810204282402992,0.052486974745988846,0.06075504794716835,-0.04958094656467438,-0.01493037585169077,-0.06947742402553558,0.13262777030467987,-0.05137885361909866,0.016075637191534042,0.01000366359949112,-0.0043238746002316475,0.056372709572315216,-0.05196155980229378,0.03574594110250473,0.041000787168741226,-0.014487438835203648,-0.03703649714589119,0.07039359211921692,-0.0004205484001431614,0.03267350420355797,0.06080803647637367,0.0